\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Independent signs with an exchanged reflection}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Take the function algebra on
#{\Omega=\{+1,-1\}^2} over #{k}, with
#{(\Theta f)(x,y)=\overline{f(y,x)}}.
Let the positive half consist of functions #{h(x)} of the
first sign, and let #{\ell} be uniform averaging over the #{4}
points. This is the commutative case of the
[algebraic reflection form](fdip-00XF).
For #{h,g} in that half,
##{B_\ell(h,g)=
 \overline{\frac{h(1)+h(-1)}2}\,
 \frac{g(1)+g(-1)}2.}
Indeed the two sign sums factor. Thus #{\ell} is reflection
positive. The nonzero function #{h(x)=x} has zero reflection
square, so the form need not be positive definite.}
